    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124-a1">

                <pb facs="0301" n="167" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg167"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    868.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Sobral to Mr. Hall.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-09-17"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 17,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the pleasure to transmit to
                    you inclosed four copies of the circular addressed by this department to the
                    prefects (jefes politicos) of the Republic, prescribing the conduct which the
                    Government ordains is to be observed by the administrative, judicial, and
                    military authorities in regard to foreigners residing in the country.</p>
                <p>Requesting that you will be able to give account thereof to your Government,</p>
                <p>I have the honor, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Martinez
                    Sobral.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
